C/ EXCLUSIVE mutual exclusion, cut-off variant (USA003087 Sec. 27.2 +
C/ Sec. 13.1/13.3).  Same contention as test_exclusive_serialized, but the
C/ contending task B is scheduled WITHOUT DEPENDENT.  B tries to CALL the
C/ EXCLUSIVE P while the primal holds it and is blocked; the primal leaves
C/ P and then reaches its own CLOSE.  Since B is not DEPENDENT, the primal
C/ halts the whole program (Sec. 13.1's overriding dependency-on-primal
C/ rule), cutting B off before it is ever granted P -- so P's body runs
C/ exactly once (the primal's use), never concurrently.  Expected:
C/ BEFORE / IN P / B CALLS / OUT P / DONE (B's own second "IN P" never
C/ prints).
 TEXCL: PROGRAM;
    P: PROCEDURE EXCLUSIVE;
       WRITE(6) 'IN P';
       WAIT 1.0;
       WRITE(6) 'OUT P';
    CLOSE P;
    B: TASK;
       WRITE(6) 'B CALLS';
       CALL P;
    CLOSE B;
    WRITE(6) 'BEFORE';
    SCHEDULE B PRIORITY(80);
    CALL P;
    WRITE(6) 'DONE';
 CLOSE TEXCL;
